+
+## 9. Spec-replay probe setup (round 1 of 12, 2026-10-12)
+
+Probe is `bench/spec_replay.py OUTDIR LABEL SAMPLING [extra server args...]`. It takes the
+production `cmd` from `serving/llama-swap.bonsai-2-27b.yaml` verbatim, points it at :8089,
+sets `LLAMA_ATTN_ROT_DISABLE=1`, and appends the extra args. Four phases each on a FRESH
+server (n-gram pool persists across requests, so a single server would inflate acceptance):
+single-agent, single-mem, dual-agent (agent fg slot 0, mem bg slot 1), dual-mem (mem fg
+slot 1, agent bg slot 0).
+
+Per-request `max_tokens = max(recorded predicted_n, floor)` with floor 768 agent / 1024
+mem, identical in every arm. Greedy sampling: `temperature 0, top_k 1, seed 0` both roles.
+Prod sampling: agent `temperature 1.0, top_p 0.95, top_k 20`; mem `temperature 0.2`; `seed 0`.
+
+**Config choice (B).** A = `--spec-type ngram-mod` with the fork's defaults — this is the
+variant the live entry would get (engine-review's ngram-mod is the candidate for deployment).
+B = `--spec-type ngram-mod --spec-draft-n-max 8`. Rationale: `ngram-mod` is the spec-type
+we'd deploy, so B keeps it and only varies the primary tunable — the draft-window length.
+The fork default is `--spec-draft-n-max 3` (m1-notes §2), a small window; on the repeated
+agent/mem traffic here, a longer window (8) is the natural way to see whether more draft
+tokens improve acceptance and decode tok/s. B is therefore a *deployment-relevant* variant
+rather than a different spec-family, so the A-vs-B comparison directly informs the deploy
+setting.
+
+**mmproj.** Per §3 the static analysis says spec + mmproj is fine for text-only traffic, to
+be confirmed empirically (`draft_n > 0`). If the spec config is refused, the script (a)
+only falls back to `LABEL-nommproj` on an explicit `refused` status — other failures (OOM,
+health timeout) are noted and exit non-zero rather than being mislabelled; (b) aborts if
+:8089 already answers before launch (stale server); (c) reads `timings.draft_n`/
+`draft_n_accepted` with a `0` default (the fork omits those fields when `n_draft_tokens == 0`),
+so every foreground row carries integer `draft_n`/`draft_n_accepted`.
+
+**Analysis note (advisor, 2026-10-12).** Count `finish_reason=length` per arm and report
+speedups both with and without capped/looping outputs, since greedy (temp 0) long loops
+inflate n-gram gains. For mem, 7 of the 12 requests are mem0-r0 step 0 (mem set has no
+mem0-r2 requests) and the fixed ~33.6k-char ADDITIVE prompt dominates, so mem n-gram
+results mostly reflect that one shared system prompt.
